  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Policies for the green and sustainable transformation of industry in Egypt</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Policies for the green and sustainable transformation of industry in Egypt.  This project aims at supporting the Egyptian government towards the green and sustainable transformation of industries via an in-depth analysis of the sector using the EQuIP Toolkit and the subsequent formulation of two policy interventions. By leveraging the GIZ Private Sector Development and Innovation Project II, which aims at improving the competitive situation of the Egyptian industry in light of increasing market requirements for a green transformation of the economy, the project will target a wide range of relevant stakeholders via policy advice and capacity development activities. The collaboration between UNIDO and GIZ aims to align efforts within a green economy framework, ultimately contributing to inclusive and sustainable industrial development in Egypt.</narrative>
  </description>
